OL,3,CProgramme listings for MON 29 DEC
OL,4,G1300FClassical Live
OL,5,     GElizabeth Alker introduces an
OL,6,     Gafternoon of specially made
OL,7,     Grecordings including Berlioz's
OL,8,     Gmusical portrait of the young
OL,9,     GChrist and a celebration of the
OL,10,     GNew Generation Artists.
OL,11,G1600FComposer of the Week: Icons of
OL,12,     FBritish Light Music
OL,13,     GDonald Macleod explores how light
OL,14,     Gmusic emerged from the theatre
OL,15,     Gpits of late-19th-century Britain
OL,16,     Gand began to find audiences in
OL,17,     Gconcert halls, music halls and at
OL,18,     Ghome.
OL,23,Vppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppp
